## Assumptions

- Verilator 4.038 does not accept `--binary` / `--timing`; the existing `tests/test_nonblock_banked.py` flow `--cc --exe --build` plus a C++ `main` is the compatible target.
- `clk_i` / `rst_n` become top-level TB inputs; the new C++ driver toggles them and calls `eval()`.
- Scenario 3 uses FQ only, one burst, 4 beats. W is offered before AW; AW is withheld until fixed cycle 20. This exercises the empty-owner-queue guard.
- Scenario 4 uses FQ only, 12 one-beat bursts (>8 AW). DS AW sink is always ready; WREADY is held low until fixed cycle 100, then allowed only when at least one AW is outstanding. This exercises producer-side AW backpressure without deadlocking on `>8 AW` handshakes.
- Scenario 1 remains the old-baseline FQ reproducer. Scenario 2 remains the five-producer concurrent test.
- The generator’s PQ AWID 4 is treated as the DS contract only. This is not a full PQ producer/ID/length validation.
- The source list is unchanged from the current script, which is already known to exist.

